esponding order:\n\n$$\nF={{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nLet $P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, carrying out the necessary matrix multiplication, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & -30 \\\\ 24 & 28\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0de063b2-395e-543a-987f-5a9f09cd0abc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553605 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7579ab44-bd79-5efe-b0c2-f284657c4cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 4 \\\\ 15 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349527} {:answer/id #uuid "8e42582e-5cb4-5323-a399-3b20a65879bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}13 & -12 \\\\ 10 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349729} {:answer/id #uuid "bb84f3e0-0aaf-50c7-8d43-3326b2bff35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350116} {:answer/id #uuid "e07ef508-ba37-54d5-9f11-5ede72a99e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350419} {:answer/id #uuid "e861d1eb-9875-5c71-862e-3da22156c169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -13 \\\\ 9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350480}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349729} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b0b11ff-0df6-52af-aa76-996c6a221114" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "725672f2-a45d-5f52-bf51-6290d583f846" :question/math-academy-id "q-81215" :question/problem "Find a $2\\times 2$ matrix $S$ that has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ and corresponding eigenvectors\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of $S,$ then $S$ must be diagonalizable.\n\nSo, we can write $S=PD{P}^{-1},$ where $P$ is a matrix whose columns are the eigenvectors of $S,$ and $D$ is a diagonal matrix whose entries are the eigenvalues in the corresponding order:\n\n$$\nS={{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nLet $P=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, carrying out the necessary matrix multiplication, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 1 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 & -12 \\\\ 10 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1d688f90-2156-50fe-abce-767206c2a691"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553647 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f13d971-9265-51dc-ba11-ae2ddbe5134a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322147} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb2f5e6-516f-5722-8eb5-dac98c70a330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-32 & -12 \\\\ 12 & -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322383} {:answer/id #uuid "c90e3b36-b996-5161-8084-e491b59e729b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322713} {:answer/id #uuid "ec347ab6-adc8-5ea1-bec1-f80c82d90acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 48 \\\\ 12 & 32\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323000} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7b780c-5ca5-52ec-97db-7fc97d7bcf98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-32 & 72 \\\\ -24 & 52\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323033} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c8c700d-19c2-58d3-8524-ed5379c8ddea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2975c4f9-6dee-5125-bb13-6ec3dea74ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-37601" :question/problem "Find ${M}^{16},$ where\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have been given the following diagonalization of $M.$\n\n$$\nM={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $M=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${M}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{M}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{16} & =P{D}^{16}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{bmatrix}}^{16}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}(\\sqrt[8]{2})^{16} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[4]{2})^{16}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 48 \\\\ 4 & 32\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-32 & 72 \\\\ -24 & 52\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8de53475-1851-510f-9270-5e2d806f8abb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553664}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553664 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1308c66e-451d-5de7-9708-faebf7ad18d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 24 \\\\ 18 & 40\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487608} {:answer/id #uuid "97e9238d-faff-5840-bb3c-d9b59bc98c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487852} {:answer/id #uuid "a6de871b-6bde-5f4b-84f9-b6d3cc4d1298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 12 \\\\ 30 & 26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487879} {:answer/id #uuid "c689ce95-133d-55c0-9ab7-8f7fcb3be04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 12 \\\\ -30 & 26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487945} {:answer/id #uuid "fb917ad6-d3d5-590e-b43c-bf793f4df7ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -12 \\\\ -30 & -26\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487945} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d99442-fd68-5c6b-a534-caad6d1d2c1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "deae4223-84c9-5248-9dcf-afbc4aa0a08d" :question/math-academy-id "q-37623" :question/problem "Find a $2\\times 2$ matrix $G$ that has eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8,$ and corresponding eigenvectors\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of $G,$ then $G$ must be diagonalizable.\n\nSo, we can write $G=PD{P}^{-1},$ where $P$ is a matrix whose columns are the eigenvectors of $G,$ and $D$ is a diagonal matrix whose entries are the eigenvalues in the corresponding order:\n\n$$\nG={{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & {v}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nLet $P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, carrying out the necessary matrix multiplication, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 24 \\\\ 18 & 40\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 12 \\\\ -30 & 26\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b6db807e-2397-57e2-bc90-d8c26b85b92f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553666}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553666 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58326d64-94a0-5d30-9f8a-711770cc7b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321839} {:answer/id #uuid "7dff0cab-c0e4-5934-b8bc-38a8ac7cb9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322139} {:answer/id #uuid "9173f37e-7ca8-5755-8f65-d0448cc8a524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322301} {:answer/id #uuid "c26c6694-bac3-5b4b-a659-172946c84d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322656} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7928ff-e4df-5e4d-b07b-7a9d64713e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322656} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebedc39f-8a4f-5591-ae46-35130d303b44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2c8cda82-c43a-5e00-b3a6-861564481ae4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37625" :question/problem "Find ${A}^{69}$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have been given the following diagonalization of $A.$\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $A=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${A}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{A}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{69} & =P{D}^{69}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{69}{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{1}^{69} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (-1)^{69}\\end{bmatrix}(\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bea2a768-29f7-5eb9-ac35-6df016064c43" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553605}}] :activity/title "Properties of Diagonalization" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552860}]}
